-- Passage rg4-story-details-inference-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('7119c905-b04e-5530-ab70-91b8150c003e', 'rg4-story-details-inference-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-story-details-inference'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Penalty Kick$q$, $q$Priya was the best kicker on the Comets. When the referee called a penalty kick in the last minute of the game, everyone expected her to take it. The score was tied, two to two.

Priya walked toward the ball. Then she stopped. Behind her stood Wen, the newest player on the team. Wen had practiced penalty kicks every day after school for a month. Priya had seen her kicking ball after ball at the empty net until the sun went down. But Wen had not scored a single goal all season.

Priya picked up the ball and held it out. "You take it," she said.

Wen's eyes went wide. "Me? What if I miss?"

"Then you miss," Priya said. "You've earned the chance."

Coach Barros raised his eyebrows, but he nodded. Wen set the ball on the white spot. She took four steps back, just like at practice. Her kick sailed low and hard into the left corner of the net.

The Comets won, three to two. Wen's teammates lifted her onto their shoulders. Priya cheered the loudest of all.

Later, Wen's mother found Priya by the bench. She did not say much. She just held Priya's hand in both of hers and shook it for a long time.$q$, 'draft')
