-- Passage rg4-text-structure-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('611d0a78-c067-5026-b642-7ac624243ed9', 'rg4-text-structure-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Frog or Toad?$q$, $q$Frogs and toads look a lot alike. Both are amphibians, which means they start life in water and later live on land. Both lay eggs, and both eat insects. Still, there are many ways to tell them apart.

One difference is their skin. A frog has smooth, wet skin that feels slimy. A toad, on the other hand, has dry, bumpy skin.

Their legs are different too. Frogs have long back legs made for big jumps. Toads have shorter legs, so they take small hops or even walk.

Where they live is another difference. Most frogs stay close to ponds and streams. Toads can live farther from water, in gardens and fields.

So the next time you see one of these animals, look closely. Its skin and legs will give you a clue about what it is.$q$, 'draft')
