-- Passage rg4-text-structure-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f918bebd-4dd6-5d30-bd12-b940f4ba8f99', 'rg4-text-structure-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Soccer and Basketball$q$, $q$Soccer and basketball are two of the most popular team sports in the world. In some ways they are alike, but in other ways they are very different.

Both games have the same goal: score more points than the other team. In both sports, players pass a ball to teammates and try to get it past defenders. Both games also need players who can run for a long time without getting tired.

The biggest difference is how players move the ball. In soccer, players mostly use their feet. Only the goalkeeper may catch the ball with the hands during play. In basketball, however, players use their hands to dribble, pass, and shoot.

The size of the playing area is different, too. A soccer field is long and grassy. A basketball court is much smaller and usually indoors.

Scoring is not the same either. A soccer goal counts as one point. In basketball, a shot can be worth one, two, or three points.$q$, 'draft')
