-- Passage rg4-theme-summary-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('81088546-0e58-5854-a332-3c31b695fa21', 'rg4-theme-summary-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-theme-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Crash Notes$q$, $q$For science class, Ms. Haddad gave each pair of students five sheets of paper. "Build a plane that flies as far as you can," she said. "Keep notes on every test."

Nadia and Jun folded their first plane quickly. It had long, pointed wings. Nadia threw it hard. It shot up, flipped over and crashed nose first, just two steps away.

"That was terrible," Jun said, crumpling it.

"Wait," Nadia said. She smoothed it out. "Let's write down what happened. Maybe it can tell us something."

They noticed the front was too light. On the second plane, they folded the nose down twice to add weight. It flew farther, but it curved to the left. They looked closely and saw that one wing was bent. On the third plane, they made the wings even. It glided straight across the gym.

Each time, they changed only one thing and wrote down the result. Their notebook filled with arrows, numbers and drawings.

On test day, their plane sailed past the center line of the gym. It came in second place. Another pair's plane flew one step farther.

Jun shrugged. "We didn't win."

Nadia held up the notebook. "But we know exactly why our plane flies," she said. "Our crashes taught us that."

Ms. Haddad looked at the pages and nodded. She asked them to share their notes with the class.$q$, 'draft')
