  ('8696fc9b-9c92-55a3-bd0a-d21eb142a539', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The words "flightless," "helpless," and "unprotected" all describe things that are missing. Which word part in "unprotected" does the same job as -less in "helpless"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The letters pro, which mean \"forward\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-word-part"},{"text":"The prefix un-, which means \"not\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"The root protect, which means \"guard\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-root-with-affix"},{"text":"The ending -ed, which shows the past","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-inflection-with-affix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The prefix un-, which means "not"$q$, $q$In "unprotected," the prefix un- shows that protection is missing, just as -less shows that help is missing in "helpless." The ending -ed only shows the word's form, so it does not tell that something is missing.$q$, 'draft', 'b654ee9c-5516-5f64-accf-ac06a3ee8a71')
