   $q$The prefix re- can mean "back" or "again," and trace means "follow a path." What did Hana do when she "retraced her steps"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She counted how many steps it was to the park","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"She took a brand new way home from school","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"She went back over the places she had been","is_correct":true},{"text":"She drew a map of her house on some paper","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She went back over the places she had been$q$, $q$Retraced means "followed the path again," and Hana thought back over Friday and went back to the park. Taking a new way home leaves out the "back" or "again" meaning of re-.$q$, 'draft', '87913974-cff1-52fc-beb0-5ddf5c00a8c3')
