insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('e4fc39df-1564-5164-8cc4-8ea3898a4fc3', 'rg4-word-parts-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Kite Festival$q$, $q$Every spring, the town of Willow Bend holds a kite festival at the beach. This year, Kofi and his cousin Marisol decided to build their own kite.

They used thin sticks, paper, and strong string. Marisol measured each stick twice. "If the sticks are uneven, the kite will tip to one side," she said. Kofi painted a bright orange sun on the paper.

On festival morning, the wind was gentle. Kofi ran down the sand, but the kite dipped and crashed. He frowned and wanted to quit right away. Marisol shook her head. "Let's rewrap the tail and try again," she said. They wound a longer tail of ribbons around the bottom stick.

On the next try, the kite rose high above the waves. It looked weightless as it floated over the crowd. A judge walked by and wrote something on a clipboard.

At the end of the day, the judge announced the winners. Kofi and Marisol won a prize for the most colorful homemade kite. Kofi admitted that he had been impatient that morning. He was glad his cousin had stayed so hopeful.$q$, 'draft')
