insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('cc28ead5-37a5-5801-bf08-7a4658d089d5', 'rg5-argument-evidence-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-argument-evidence'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Recess Should Come Before Lunch$q$, $q$At Brookside Elementary, students eat lunch first and then go outside for recess. I think we should switch the order. Recess should come before lunch.

The first reason is that students would eat more of their food. Right now, many students rush through lunch so they can get outside sooner. Last month, our student council weighed the food left on trays for one week. Students threw away about 40 pounds of fruit and vegetables each day.

The second reason is that students would behave better in the lunchroom. After running around, students are hungry and ready to sit down. At Ridgeview School across town, recess was moved before lunch two years ago. The principal there reported that lunchroom arguments dropped by half.

The third reason is that students would return to class calmer. Ms. Okafor, a fourth grade teacher, kept a chart for two weeks. On days when her class had a short outdoor break before lunch, she needed fewer minutes to get everyone settled for math.

Some people say students will be too tired to eat. However, a short rest happens naturally while students wash their hands and line up.

Switching the order costs nothing, and it could help everyone. Brookside should give it a try.$q$, 'draft')
