   $q$Which evidence supports the point that playing several sports protects young bodies?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rosa Delgado found that volleyball quickly became her favorite.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Seven out of ten players who quit said the sport stopped being fun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Swimming builds strong lungs and gymnastics improves balance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"One-sport athletes were about twice as likely to get overuse injuries.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One-sport athletes were about twice as likely to get overuse injuries.$q$, $q$The study of 1,200 athletes is about injuries, so it backs up the point about protecting bodies. The survey of players who quit supports the point about fun.$q$, 'draft', 'a5e8df0e-db30-546a-a37c-79fc3d774e8b')
