values ('927d0d43-a5aa-575f-b678-4b5a65e396bf', 'rg5-authors-purpose-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The New Skate Park on Elm Street$q$, $q$Account 1: From the School News Blog, by Kofi Mensah, Grade 5

The new skate park on Elm Street opened on Saturday, and it is the best thing to happen to our town in years. Before, my friends and I had to ride in parking lots, where drivers honked at us. Now we have smooth ramps, a long rail, and a bowl shaped like a giant bathtub. I landed my first kickflip on opening day. Older skaters even showed the younger kids how to fall safely. I hope the town builds a second park on the other side of the river.

Account 2: A Letter to the Town Council from Harriet Lindqvist, Elm Street Resident

I have lived across from the old empty lot for thirty years. I am glad young people finally have a safe place to skate. However, the park has caused some problems for my street. The sound of wheels on concrete starts early in the morning and goes on until dark. On weekends, visitors park their cars in front of my driveway. I ask the council to set park hours from nine in the morning to eight at night. I also ask for a small parking area so visitors do not block our homes.$q$, 'draft')
