-- Passage rg5-authors-purpose-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f8f17a23-dd06-5264-814b-5745aec74576', 'rg5-authors-purpose-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Bikes for Rent on Linden Street$q$, $q$Account 1: Blog Post by Priya Nair, Nurse

I now ride a rental bike to the hospital three days a week. I unlock it with a code on my phone and drop it at a station near the front door. It saves me bus fare and gives me fresh air before a long shift. There is one problem. When I arrive at the Linden Street station at seven in the morning, it is sometimes empty. Then I have to walk to the next station or catch the bus after all.

Account 2: Letter from Walter Brennan, Bakery Owner

The new bike station sits right in front of my bakery. To make room for it, the city removed four parking spaces. Some longtime customers say they cannot find a place to park, so they shop somewhere else. On the other hand, I now see riders stop in for a muffin on their way to work. I hope the city will find a way to bring back some parking nearby.

Account 3: Update from the City Transportation Office

In its first month, the bike program had 30 stations and more than 1,200 rides. The busiest station was Linden Street, near the hospital. Riders reported that some stations run out of bikes in the early morning. Starting next month, a truck will move extra bikes to busy stations before seven. The city is also studying parking needs for shops near the stations.$q$, 'draft')
