-- Passage rg5-character-setting-plot-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('40882754-264f-5b41-b0c5-c403af00844d', 'rg5-character-setting-plot-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Kite Contest$q$, $q$Every spring, the town of Pine Hollow held a kite contest in the big field behind the library. This year, Dev Patel and his cousin Lucia Moreno entered together.

Dev had made his kite from a kit. He followed each step in the booklet and checked the pictures twice. His kite was a neat red diamond with a perfect tail.

Lucia had built hers from scratch. She used old newspaper, two bamboo sticks and a ribbon from her sister's birthday present. It was lopsided, and one corner was taped three times.

When the whistle blew, the wind was gusty and wild. Dev's kite rose smoothly at first. Then a strong gust spun it in circles, and it crashed into the grass. Dev stood still and stared at the booklet, but it said nothing about wind like this.

Lucia's kite dipped and wobbled. She did not panic. She pulled it down, tore off a piece of the tail and tried again. Then she added a strip of ribbon. On her fourth try, the kite climbed high and stayed there.

Dev walked over. "How did you know what to change?" he asked.

"I didn't," Lucia said with a grin. "I just kept trying things."

Neither cousin won a prize. But on the walk home, Dev asked if they could build the next kite together, without a booklet.$q$, 'draft')
