-- Passage rg5-character-setting-plot-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('e96e7368-c066-54a1-85b4-0b4b28de3f8a', 'rg5-character-setting-plot-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Heron and the Kingfisher$q$, $q$On the edge of a wide marsh lived a heron and a kingfisher. Both birds fished in the same shallow water, but they fished in very different ways.

The kingfisher was quick and proud. She darted from branch to branch, diving at every flash of silver she saw. Often she came up with nothing but a beak full of mud. "At least I am trying," she would chirp, shaking her feathers dry.

The heron was slow and quiet. He stood on one leg in the reeds for long stretches, as still as a fence post. When a fish finally swam close, he struck once and rarely missed.

One summer, a dry spell shrank the marsh to a few small pools. The fish grew scarce and hid in the shade. The kingfisher dove again and again, growing more tired each day. The heron waited by the deepest pool and caught enough to eat.

At last the kingfisher landed beside him, too weary to fly. "How do you find fish when there are none?" she asked.

"I do not find them," said the heron. "I let them find me."

The next morning, the kingfisher perched on a low branch and watched the water before she dove. She caught a fish on her very first try.$q$, 'draft')
