insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('df709026-dabb-548e-bf1c-7d3e82bcbee1', 'rg5-comparing-texts-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$New Kid, New Friends$q$, $q$Text 1: The Chess Club (realistic fiction)

Farid had been at his new school for two weeks, and he still spoke very little English. At lunch, he sat alone and watched other kids laugh at jokes he did not understand.

One day he saw a sign with a picture of a chessboard. Back home, Farid had played chess with his grandfather every evening. He went to the club after school and sat across from a girl named Rosa. They could not talk much. But when Farid moved his knight and trapped her queen, Rosa's eyes went wide. "Again!" she said, setting up the pieces.

By the end of the month, Farid had six new friends. He was learning English, and they were learning his best chess tricks.

Text 2: Rice Balls (realistic fiction)

On her first day in a new country, Aiko opened her lunch box. Inside were two rice balls wrapped in seaweed. A boy at her table wrinkled his nose. Aiko quickly closed the lid.

For a week she ate in the library, hiding her food. Then her teacher, Mr. Okafor, announced a class food day. Aiko almost stayed home. Instead, she and her mother made a big plate of rice balls.

At the food table, the same boy picked one up and took a careful bite. "Hey, this is really good," he said. "Can you show me how to make these?" Aiko smiled. For the first time, her lunch felt like something to share instead of something to hide.$q$, 'draft')
