   $q$Why might the author of Text 2 have chosen to let the team finish second instead of first?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that swimming is a harder sport than basketball and is much harder to win.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that Wen was not ready to swim and should practice more before the next meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"To show that Tomas was right and the coach should have let him swim the last leg.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-author-purpose"},{"text":"To show that helping a teammate is worthwhile even when it does not lead to a win.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that helping a teammate is worthwhile even when it does not lead to a win.$q$, $q$Even without a win, Wen swims "her best time ever" and Tomas feels proud, so the lesson does not depend on winning, unlike in Text 1. The story never says Tomas should have swum instead; his feelings change.$q$, 'draft', 'aba426a3-e8ac-591a-a5bf-09b601eb3e1a')
