insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d6a69aac-0bba-5872-9324-113523ecba23', 'rg5-comparing-texts-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Worth the Wait$q$, $q$Text 1: The Crow and the Mango Tree (a fable)

A young crow found a mango tree full of green fruit. "I will eat them all today," he cawed. He pecked mango after mango, but each one was hard and sour. By evening, he had a stomachache, and the ground was covered with spoiled fruit.

An old crow watched from a nearby branch. "Wait two weeks," she said. The young crow grumbled, but he waited. When he returned, the mangoes were golden and sweet. There were enough for every bird in the forest.

Moral: Good things come to those who wait.

Text 2: The Little Silver Fish (a folktale)

A fisherman named Kwame cast his net each morning. One day, he caught a tiny silver fish. "Please let me go," said the fish. "I am too small to feed you now. Come back in a year, and I will be big."

Kwame thought about it. A tiny fish would not make much of a meal. He opened the net, and the fish swam away.

A year later, Kwame cast his net in the same spot. He pulled up a fish so large that his whole village had a feast. As they ate, Kwame told the story of the little fish. From then on, the village fishers always threw the small fish back.$q$, 'draft')
