-- Passage rg5-comparing-texts-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a6cafceb-3f38-52a4-897b-8c5817f144f6', 'rg5-comparing-texts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Happy Accidents$q$, $q$Text 1: The Wrong Turn (realistic fiction)

At the spring recital, Lucia danced in the front row. Halfway through the song, she turned left when everyone else turned right. For a moment she froze. Then she remembered what her teacher always said: "Keep moving."

Lucia spun all the way around, as if she had planned it, and stepped back into line. The audience clapped even louder.

Afterward, her teacher, Ms. Adeyemi, gave her a hug. "That spin was better than my idea," she said. "Let's add it to the dance for next year."

Text 2: The Cracked Bowl (realistic fiction)

Ravi spent two weeks making a clay bowl for his mother's birthday. When it came out of the kiln, a long crack ran down one side. Ravi wanted to throw it away.

His grandfather turned the bowl slowly in his hands. "In some places, people fix broken pottery and paint the cracks gold," he said. "They believe the repair makes the bowl more special."

Together they glued the crack and painted it with gold paint. Ravi's mother loved the bowl. She set it on the kitchen windowsill, where the gold line caught the morning light.$q$, 'draft')
